  "notes": "FIRST PocketRoofline measurement on smartphone-class silicon (iPhone 13 / A15). Radios fully off (airplane mode, Wi-Fi and Bluetooth disabled), unplugged, app in foreground, single session run back-to-back SISO -> LISO -> SILO with one unrecorded warmup and ~3 s between repeats. PROTOCOL DEVIATION, recorded per METHODOLOGY 5: the device began at thermalState 'fair', not 'nominal' (the 10-minute ambient cooldown was not achieved before the session), and never returned to nominal. These are therefore warm-start figures. They are published as measured; the cold-start protocol run is a separate future session and will not overwrite this one. Stable regime and the control for the whole session: decode sd 0.37 t/s (0.9% CV) across 5 repeats, 95% CI [42.53, 43.08] t/s. Because decode is this reproducible here, the decline measured under sustained load in SILO cannot be attributed to measurement noise."
